cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use swelter, please cite it using this metadata."
title: "swelter"
abstract: >-
  A community-owned network of low-cost heat and air-quality sensors with the
  pipeline, calibration, and accessible map that make its readings trustworthy
  and open. Nodes measure temperature, humidity, PM2.5/PM10, optional NO2, and a
  derived heat index; a time-series pipeline ingests the readings, QC-flags the
  bad ones, calibrates each node's drift against reference monitors, and maps
  urban heat islands and AQI at neighborhood resolution through a framework-free
  WCAG 2.2 AA dashboard. Observation data is open (CC0-1.0) and exports through
  open standards (CSV, JSON, the read-only OGC SensorThings subset, and a
  Datasette-openable store). Privacy invariants are merge-blocking: no field can
  identify or locate a person, public coordinates snap to a coarse grid, and
  calibrated and raw readings are never silently mixed.
type: software
